<title>JAPAN: Japan external reserves $222.247 bln at end-July.</title>
<headline>Japan external reserves $222.247 bln at end-July.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's external reserves fell $58 million  from a month earlier to $222.247 billion at the end of July, the Ministry  of Finance (MOF) said on Friday.</p>
<p>Reserves at the end of June were $222.305 billion, up $544 million  from the previous month.</p>
<p>--Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-3432-9780</p>
</text>
